   "dahlquist_note": "Under floor, euler/heun2/rk38 hit dahlquist error 4.539993e-05, which equals exp(-10), the full reference value: the Q15 state decays to exactly 0 and the true answer is below one LSB, so floor's downward bias lands on the right answer. Under round-to-nearest the state stalls in a dead zone above zero (errors 0.033 to 0.092, up to 2032x worse).",
   "mechanism": "Each Q15 multiply floors, injecting a -0.5 LSB expected bias per product. rk4 spends more multiplies per unit of simulated time and takes larger steps at equal budget, so its order advantage is spent absorbing bias; cheap low-order methods take more, smaller steps and win on problems whose solutions decay."
