 "rc_thermal_collapse": {
  "verdict": "All 8 classical methods land within 1.6% of one another on rc_thermal under floor (errors 0.1558 to 0.1582) because every one of them drives the Q15 state into a dead zone 4 to 18 LSBs from the origin while the true solution still has norm 0.1592: the reported error is essentially the reference itself, a quantization floor, not a method property. Under round-to-nearest the same methods separate (rk38 reaches 0.0511), and the best discovered method reaches 0.0461 while still using floor.",
