   },
   "mechanism": "rc_thermal decays toward equilibrium and its derivative is stored scaled by 1/8 (DERIV_SCALE), so late in the run the quantized derivative terms are a few LSBs; floor rounding turns them into extra decay, and every classical method's state collapses to near zero instead of tracking the slow mode. Error metric is ||y - ref(4)||/peak, so everyone reports about ||ref(4)|| = 0.159 minus a small residual."
